i@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/35/321935/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I2cd4a12a52dafd17b4eb3287cb23f539c765d73e" commit="02759e9506c93aea3a27b80cbf1a84c1558b945c" commit_message="A a WAR for incorrect tx duration calculation,  accept bss channel survey data  if  (tx_delta + rx_delta) is higher  than busy_delat by 2% or less. if higher make busy_delta = (tx_delta + rx_delta).  BUG=b/23723272 TEST=Manually verified with iw that normal survey data is returned from driver     and there is no regression. Actual bug needs to be verified in the field     as the bug only repros in the field.  Change-Id: I2cd4a12a52dafd17b4eb3287cb23f539c765d73e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/322263 Commit-Ready: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Julan Hsu &lt;julanhsu@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="322263" owner_email="sduvvuri@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/63/322263/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I0f7e5406218246762597edf73d04b59fdbf94e90" commit="09e5fd271e7d189d1cf72d4be93bad05dc370e2c" commit_message="Disable buffet tests  BUG:550826 TEST=None  Change-Id: I0f7e5406218246762597edf73d04b59fdbf94e90 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/322223 Commit-Ready: Vitaly Buka &lt;vitalybuka@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Vitaly Buka &lt;vitalybuka@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Alex Vakulenko &lt;avakulenko@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="322223" owner_email="vitalybuka@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/23/322223/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I82e8dcc6f3d486e7e9db7b086b41bb6e7f74ce00" commit="5e3f8277b41e849e94e49488738b72199f19f45d" commit_message="CHROMIUM: wakeup: Clear wakeup_type in userspace  This allows userspace to clear /sys/power/wakeup_type instead of doing it in the kernel. If an automatic wakeup cancels suspend, we don't want to fully resume the system. When clearing it in the kernel, we wouldn't be able to tell this happened, though. This is because the wakeup_type could be user from a wakeup before suspend was initiated. It would not change from an automatic wakeup, so userspace would not know about the automatic wakeup.  Backported from 3.18 patch e9f06607d891d6c739b6b6611f77b03bbd7b8e3a.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:47095 TEST=on glados: echo 1 &gt; /usr/share/power_manager/suspend_to_idle restart powerd echo automatic &gt; /sys/class/rtc/rtc0/device/power/wakeup_type echo +10 &gt; /sys/class/rtc/rtc0/wakealarm; echo unknown &gt; \ /sys/power/wakeup_type; powerd_dbus_suspend -check that /sys/power/wakeup_type is automatic after the system wakes from the rtc alarm.  Conflicts:  drivers/base/power/wakeup.c  include/linux/suspend.h  Original-Change-Id: Id4a83f70a2ac1fa66e6f5eaeb5e368cd3beac688 Original-signed-off-by: Derek Basehore &lt;dbasehore@chromium.org&gt; Original-reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/311392 Original-reviewed-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: I82e8dcc6f3d486e7e9db7b086b41bb6e7f74ce00 Signed-off-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320434 Reviewed-by: Derek Basehore &lt;dbasehore@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="320434" owner_email="ejcaruso@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" p